var e={binary:[`Fill every empty cell with 0 or 1; the given cells cannot be changed.`,`Each row and column must contain equal numbers of 0s and 1s.`,`No three consecutive cells may contain the same digit horizontally or vertically.`,`No two complete rows or two complete columns may be identical.`],crossword:[`Fill each horizontal and vertical word using its clue.`,`Words crossing at a cell must share the same letter.`,`Keep the given letters. In a standard grid, black cells separate words and cannot be filled.`,`In a silent grid, the black cells are hidden: you must discover their positions as well as the words. Enter the hash character "#" in each cell that should be black.`,`Complete every word and, in a silent grid, mark every black cell to solve the puzzle.`],cryptarithm:[`Replace each letter with a digit so that the displayed arithmetic is correct.`,`The same letter always represents the same digit; different letters represent different digits.`,`A leading letter in a multi-digit number cannot be zero. Keep the assignments supplied as clues.`],logigram:[`Use the written clues to match items across the categories.`,`Each item has exactly one partner in each other category.`,`Mark impossible pairs with a cross and confirmed pairs with a check. All category pairings must agree with each other and the clues.`],kakuro:[`Fill each playable cell with a digit from 1 to 9.`,`A clue gives the sum of the consecutive white cells to its right or below it.`,`Do not repeat a digit within one horizontal or vertical run. Every crossing cell must satisfy both sums.`,`Keep any given digits. The puzzle is solved when every cell is filled and all runs satisfy their clues.`],loto:[`Draw one number at a time. Each number can be drawn only once.`,`Drawn numbers are marked on every ticket where they appear; empty ticket cells are ignored.`,`The game is complete when every numbered cell on all displayed tickets has been drawn.`],mastermind:[`Find the hidden sequence of colors within the available attempts.`,`Fill a whole row and check the guess. A color may occur more than once in the secret code.`,`Exact matches count pegs with the correct color and position. Misplaced matches count correct colors in other positions; each secret peg is counted at most once.`,`Use the feedback to refine the next guess. You win when every peg is in the correct position.`],sudoku:[`Fill each empty cell with a digit from 1 to 9.`,`Each row, column and 3 by 3 box must contain every digit exactly once.`,`Given digits cannot be changed. Complete the grid without a repetition to solve the puzzle.`],yakazu:[`Fill each white cell with a number. Black cells separate horizontal and vertical runs.`,`A run of N white cells must contain the numbers 1 through N, each exactly once.`,`A crossing cell belongs to both runs and must satisfy both. Keep the given numbers and complete all runs.`],memory:[`Reveal two cards and try to find matching pairs.`,`Matching cards stay face up. Unmatched cards turn face down again after a short delay.`,`Remember the revealed cards and find every pair to finish the game.`],puzzle:[`Reassemble the image by placing every piece in its correct position.`,`Move pieces by dragging them. Use the piece menu to rotate them by the angles allowed for the selected shape.`,`Match both the picture and the edges. Finish when every piece has the correct position and orientation.`],tangram:[`Reproduce the target silhouette using all seven pieces.`,`Move and rotate the pieces; flip a piece when necessary.`,`The pieces must cover the target without gaps or overlaps.`],solitaire:[`Move all cards to the four foundations, building each suit from Ace to King.`,`Build tableau columns in descending rank with alternating colors. You may move an ordered face-up sequence together.`,`Only a King or a sequence starting with a King may enter an empty tableau column.`,`Turn over exposed face-down cards and draw from the stock to make more cards available.`],chess:[`White and Black take turns. The aim is to checkmate the opposing king: attack it so that no legal move escapes the attack.`,`Kings move one square; queens along ranks, files and diagonals; rooks along ranks and files; bishops along diagonals. Knights jump two squares in one direction and one perpendicular.`,`Pawns advance forward and capture diagonally. From their starting rank they may advance two squares; on the last rank they promote. Castling and en passant are available only when the position permits them.`,`You may not leave your own king in check. Stalemate and other drawn positions end the game without a winner. A loaded position may begin with either side to move.`],checkers:[`This game uses international draughts on a 10 by 10 board. Play on the dark squares; the side to move is indicated below the board.`,`Men move one square diagonally forward and capture by jumping an opposing piece in either direction. Kings move and capture along diagonals over any available distance.`,`Capturing is compulsory. When several capture sequences are possible, choose one that takes the greatest number of pieces and complete the whole sequence.`,`A man becomes a king when it finishes its turn on the last rank. Win by leaving the opponent without pieces or legal moves.`],wari:[`This game uses Oware Abapa rules: each player owns six pits. A normal starting board has four seeds in each pit.`,`Choose a nonempty pit on your side and sow its seeds one by one around the board, skipping the starting pit on a complete circuit.`,`If the final seed leaves an opposing pit with two or three seeds, capture them. Continue backwards through consecutive opposing pits containing two or three seeds.`,`You must feed an opponent with no seeds when possible. A capture that would take every opposing seed is cancelled.`,`Capture more than half the 48 seeds to win. If no feeding move remains or a position repeats three times, the remaining seeds are collected on their owners’ sides; equal scores draw.`]};export{e as GAME_RULES};
